A||||12||Joel||ALL Fiero owners, please read! ||||1||
Z||000000||Joel||12-20-2000||04:47 AM||||I would like to apologize on the behalf of most all MR2 owners for the obsurd comments from "CUTTER". Obviously, he has no respect for others or cares about what others think. I have an MR2 and am a member of the IMOC Message Board. Sure, I could sell it and buy a Toyota Supra Twin Turbo, but i chose to keep my MR2 and buy an MR2 Turbo engine. Why? Sure the Supra is an all around better car, but it's not always the performance of the car that matters. Sure, you guys could sell your Fieros and buy better cars (no matter what you have, someone ALWAYS has better) It's sometimes just the feeling you get when you drive a certain car. And I'm sure that's why you have the car you have. That's definately why I have mine. Please understand that not all MR2 owners are stuck up pricks like CUTTER. He acted out of great disrespect of the Fiero community. <P>On the other hand, some of the Fiero owners made some bad comments about the MR2 which kept CUTTER alive like "it's nothing compared to American Muscle." Since when is a V6 or 4 cylinder considered "American Muscle"? What's so Muscular about it? The bigger the engine, the heavier the car, the more upset the balance. Simple, yet so complex. Well, to followup to those comments, CUTTER could have pulled out the file in a magazine test 88MR2 Supercharged versus 88 Fiero Formula. The MR2 was beating the Fiero so bad that "it was deemed no contest as the MR2 was so much better in so many ways."-quote Car&Driver. It is little comments like that, that get so much tension and hate between two car groups. The best thing to do is IGNORE HIM! Don't try to put out fire with gasoline. WHO CARES! You have what you have and you want what you want. Please accept out apolgy. Thanks. <P><BR>P.S. If any of you felt this was to start flames, let me know what I have done incorrectly. We are not a bad group of people. It's easy for ONE single person to destroy the reputation of thousands.||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-20-2000||09:11 AM||||no body is upset... at all MR2 owners.. we just like to razz Cutter.. and it works SOO well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>Your TOTALLY right.. it's the fun of Driving the car and owning somthing strange and unusual in stead of Buying a Vette or Supra  (i used to have an 87 Turbo) and being done and having the "small member compensation" persona. the Fiero is fun and like the MR2 easy to work on (except the Turbo model it's takes 12 freeking hours to pull a bad turbo off.. been there, it sucked) <BR>anywho.. i don't think anyone here really thinks all MR2 owners are flea bags.. just the ones that are too serious about thier toys... I'm not TOTALLY sure about the other members here but my feelings are  it's a car.. get over it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> yep mines slow... yep there are MANY other cars i'd love to have... HOWEVER there are many car owners that make outragous claims about their car/it's performance/it's realiability/it's appointments that need to be put in check. and some that are just TOO much fun to rag on cause they take it SO seriously! <P><BR>Welcome to the forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  mind if i send your e-mail addy to a Friend with a 93 N/A thats getting a 95 Turbo motor installed nex week? His name is Lynn Preston... (marietta, Ga.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||12-20-2000||09:27 AM||||Joel I agreed with you until you hit the article part and the American muscle part<P>First off, any american car with torque is considered american muscle.  Since most V6s have twice the amount of torque then there counterparts 4 cyl.'s, they are considered american muscle.  Ever heard of the Grand National?<P>About the article thing.  They (R&T) were testing a supercharged MR2 against an N/A Fiero.  Of course the SC MR2 is going to be faster!  It wasn't car and driver it was Road and Track.  They mainly criticized the Fiero on bump steer and handling on rough surfaces.  They said that the suspension on the MR2 was better in those conditions, but didn't handle as well as the Fiero did on smooth surfaces.  Most of the article was about how great the supercharged engine was ("leap in technology") and the weight of the MR2 being a lot less (i.e. more nimble). IMHO it wasn't fair.  Supercharge the Fiero then test them. <P>The Car and Driver did a better article testing the MR2 (n/a), CRX, and Fiero Formula had the Fiero coming in close behind the MR2, the downfalls being stupid things like ergonomics and gauge placement.  Thats the things about those articles, you really can't place much value on them because a. they aren't the ones buying the cars (usually), b.often times personal likes and dislikes which may differ from yours are brought into account and c. no matter what they say some are more biased to certain types of cars then other.  However they are good because they provide a good idea of what an outsider might think about your car and it gives you their performance results and handling details etc.(for referencing).<P>Not flaming, just IMHO.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||12-20-2000||09:37 AM||||No hard feelings!<P>I have a Road and Track comparison test that pitted a Fiero Formula against a supercharged MR2.  R/T was impressed with the improvements Pontiac made for '88, but chose the MR2 for its outright speed and nimble handling.<P>I also have a Motorweek video in which they tested the same two cars.  They were impressed with the S/C MR2's power, but liked the Formula's handling and brakes better, and said they thought it would be easier to live with the Fiero on a daily basis.  They also noted the stiff price difference between the two cars, and said for their money, they'd take the Fiero.<P>And the great debate goes on...respectfully, of course.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||12-20-2000||09:51 AM||||Arrrgh! Make it stop! <P>As far as you needing to apologize for CUTTER so's we don't rumble, I say no need dude. The reason Mr. C got mad was entirely predictable. The way he handled it just displayed some immature coping mechanisms, but who among us is going to be called a slobbering pigf*cker and <B>NOT</B> take offense.<P>Folks, we behaved like a bunch of schoolyard bullies. We chose a target that we felt would not defend himself and/or was weaker, and attacked viciously.  GTB, man you usually go after people who beg for that kind of treatment, but this time you brought the noise. And Black88, well, I'm not surprised you jumped on the bandwagon.<P>Deos Cutter have some issues to resolve and contrition to be made? Most definately.  Does the MR2 high tribunal need to offer sacrifice to appease the great Fiero gods? Ahh, no. If some 48 post newbie now has a rager against MR2 owners, I really think y'all do have the confidence to brush it off. (except for your 48 post newbies, they can get pretty vocal, eh?)||||reg||1
Z||000005||pHoOl||12-20-2000||10:58 AM||||Okay, i first started reading about this debate last night and read all of the posts, cause i was just that bored.<P>joel-<P>I agree with you right up until you start throwing the "my supercharged car is faster than yours" argument.  Of course a supercharged car would beat a stock one, unless it was a supercharged saturn vs. a viper.  <P>To quote you, i think that in bringing up the article you were "putting out a fire with gasoline".  I don't really think that any of us on the fiero forum give a rat's azz if Road and Track thinks that your car is faster.  We like fieros because we like them.  If we wanted some sort of a super fast car, we would buy a corvette or a viper or a ferrari.  (or maybe steal one since we can't afford them)<P>you get my point.  And i think that if we keep opening threads to apologize or to fan the flames is only going to make the fire worse.  we understand that he doesn't represent MR2 owners.  He's a dick, we know, PearlBlueSoul opened i think three threads telling us this.  We don't need anymore.  Let's just drop it.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||2xsess||12-20-2000||11:59 AM||||Amen Brother pHoOl.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||fldevel||12-20-2000||02:02 PM||||sence when was the MR2 more nimble then a fiero ?? the mr2 may be a tad lighter but i still cant take corners with it like i can my fieros .. maybe others have had different experiences but i own a mr2 and ive driven sevrel others incluting turbo modles and id still go back to my fiero GT anyday. <P> and why are we still fighting about cars .. <BR>jeesh gimmi a break ..||||reg||1
