Z||000009||Fformula88||12-20-2000||03:35 PM||||This is just another case of to each his own.  Whichever car you own, your going to think is better and find arguments why.  In '88, R/T tested the fastest trim levels of each car... the Formula and the supercharged MR2.  Result was the MR2 was faster.  It depends on personal taste which one is better.  For myself, I wouldn't give up my Fiero for a SC MR2.  But I am sure people who own SC MR2's wouldn't want my Formula either.  However, since this is a Fiero messageboard, I am certain anyone making claims about how great an MR2 is, while putting down Fieros is going to be flamed big time. <P>I haven't followed the big Cutter arguments too closely.  However, I have read some of it.  There is no reason for the MR2 community to apologize.  Its not thew cars, nor the communities fault or responsibility.  He is his own man and entitled to his opinions.  What anybody says, and brings upon themselves is their own choice.  <P>But I am sure we all can appreciate the gesture of trying to keep the peace your trying to make.  I don't think anyone here will hold the MR2 community responsible for one person.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
